  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 150 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will flatten further this weekend into early next \nweek as troughing over the western US deepens. Models show two \nshortwaves, one this weekend and a potentially much stronger one by \nnext Tuesday/Wednesday, that could bring increased shower and storm \nchances over a broader portion of the area. Chances this weekend \nappear more scattered in nature as the better forcing from the \nshortwave travels largely to our north and west and the mid-level \nflow veers more substantially. The wave next week has the potential \nto bring more widespread/heavier precipitation, especially if \nmoisture from eastern Pacific tropical activity can become \ninvolved as some models suggest, but those details remain \nuncertain from this range. \n\nWith a lack of significant fronts, temperatures are forecast to \nremain well above average through the weekend and beyond, with 90s\npotentially becoming more widespread by the weekend. \n\nWare",
